## Exact projection snapshots and cache

`meridian.evidence_serialization` provides exact closed mapping conversion for
the typed evidence inventory. `meridian.projection_cache` binds one validated
inventory to exact Core source state, adapter and reader identity, projection
authorization purpose and scope, canonical JSON, a deterministic cache key, and
a content digest.

Cache creation repeats canonical verification and authorization after adapter
work. Exact replay preserves original bytes and capture time. A different output
under identical declared inputs fails as projection nondeterminism. Public cache
reads require fresh authorization before opening student-level snapshot bytes.
Current assessment distinguishes reusable, reprojection-required, historical,
and unverifiable states without rewriting historical snapshots.

These projection snapshots are derived cache entries, not report snapshots,
Grades, proficiency results, or mutable current views. See
[`docs/architecture/exact-projection-snapshots-and-cache.md`](docs/architecture/exact-projection-snapshots-and-cache.md).


## Grouping-signal preview and teacher review

Current unreleased v0.2 development includes the issue #39 review boundary.
`meridian.grouping_signal_preview` and
`meridian.grouping_signal_preview_generation` build an immutable,
content-addressed teacher-review preview from one explicit exact #38 derivation.
`meridian.grouping_signal_currentness` reuses #38 semantics read-only so stale or
blocked historical derivations remain explainable without generating replacement
state.

`meridian.grouping_signal_review`,
`meridian.grouping_signal_review_storage`, and
`meridian.grouping_signal_review_workflow` preserve deliberate teacher
`accepted_for_export` or `rejected` decisions as immutable revisions with an
explicit selected-review pointer. Acceptance requires the exact derivation to be
current at review time, no blocking diagnostics, and exact acknowledgment of all
warning diagnostic IDs.

`meridian.grouping_signal_preview_projection` provides the teacher-facing view.
Current Core roster names are joined transiently by `student_id`; names are not
persisted into #38/#39 canonical state and do not affect fingerprints or
digests. Bands remain neutral contextual labels such as `Band 1` and `Band 2`.

Previewing does not export. Accepting does not export. Export happens only in
issue #40 through Core `grouping_signal_set_v1` and optional
`grouping_signal_csv_v1`.

See
[Grouping-signal preview, diagnostics, and teacher review](docs/architecture/grouping-signal-preview-diagnostics.md).
